<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 20 July, from 1810 to 1976.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1810">1810 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bogotá rises against Spanish rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A quarrel over a borrowed flower vase sparked an uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> that created a governing junta. Colombia celebrates 20 July as its Independence Day; full independence came after Bolívar's victory in 1819.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1866">1866 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">160 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Austria defeats Italy at Lissa, the first great ironclad battle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admiral Tegetthoff's Austrian fleet defeated a larger Italian force off the island of Lissa in the Adriatic. The ramming of the Italian flagship convinced navies to fit rams to warships for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stauffenberg's bomb fails to kill Hitler</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg">Claus von Stauffenberg</a> left a briefcase bomb at Hitler's Wolf's Lair headquarters, but Hitler survived. The plotters were executed and thousands more were arrested in the reprisals that followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 11 lands on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin landed the lunar module Eagle in the Sea of Tranquillity. Hours later, at 10.56 pm US Eastern time, Armstrong stepped onto the surface, watched by some 600 million people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1976">1976 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">50 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Viking 1 makes the first successful landing on Mars</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> 1 lander touched down on Chryse Planitia and sent back the first photographs from the Martian surface. It operated for more than six years.</p></div></li></ol>
